Wow, this gives me flashbacks of early model merging. Complete insanity, I love it!

@RoliumGens has released a sub-6B sparse activation AI model built with a new architecture called fusion. It fuses weights from @liquidai's LFM2.5-2.6B and @Alibaba_Qwen's Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, achieving near Qwen3.6-35B-A3B performance while being about a fifth of the size.

This is the first model in a new series, with over six weeks of dedicated work. Two more models using this architecture are coming soon: a mini version of minimax m3 and a mini version of deepseek v4 flash, both already built. The models are 26B and 12B, and the creator seeks more compute to benchmark and improve them further, aiming to push frontier intelligence locally. They invite @0xSero to help finish the work and release these models open source, with plans to develop larger models like glm 5.2, kimi k3, and qwen 3.8.

I was so impressed with the claims for this model that I recorded an audio myself, then degraded it quite a bit, and the model held up.

@HuggingApps: "UniPASE arrived on Hugging Face to fix your bad quality voice calls. It is a speech enhancement model that can fill the gaps of a dropping connection."

I was so impressed with the claims that I had to try it myself, using my own voice.

I've been waiting for a simple way to find and set up the right local models for your hardware. The team has done it. Try it now.

@MiaAI_lab: "Claim your name. Be fast."

More developer preview slots will be released soon.

A new foundation model that reads and generates DNA sequences has been released on Hugging Face. The demo space allows users to test the model's capabilities.

@gsbenegas: "Excited to share MarinDNA, a 1B gLM that rivals Evo 2 40B on variant effect prediction while being 2,330 times faster. With @eczech0, we built around a standard Transformer so we could reuse LLM infrastructure and methods while focusing on data curation and scaling."

The linked URLs describe MarinDNA as an efficient, open-source genomic language model that combines data curation, hyperparameter transfer, and scaling techniques to achieve balanced performance across tasks.
